{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtP3VYPE2Z57mqzA8v21","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Prisma 8 is set up in the project, the tables exist in your local database, and `npx tsx script.ts` runs and prints the user with both posts. I did not commit anything.\n\n- **Version:** the npm tags are the same as your colleague's note. `prisma@latest` is 8.0.0-rc.33 and `@prisma/client@latest` is still 7.10.1. I used Prisma 8 (`prisma` 8.0.0-rc.33 and `@prisma/orm-postgres` 8.0.0-rc.23, which is also `latest`). Prisma 8 has no `@prisma/client`, so that package is not installed. Prisma 8 is a release candidate, not a stable release.\n- **Schema:** `User` has a unique `email` and an optional `name`. `Post` has `title`, optional `content`, `published` defaulting to `false`, and one author. The init scaffold had extra fields, which I removed.\n- **Tables:** created with `prisma db init`. I confirmed in Postgres that `User` has 1 row and `Post` has 2.\n- **Script:** `script.ts` creates `alice@example.com` with two posts and prints all users with their posts. A second run fails on the unique email, as expected. The script is not idempotent.\n- **Reverted:** the init command changed `tsconfig.json` and `.gitignore`. I restored both from git because the changes were not needed. The project still type-checks.\n- **Not done:** I did not run `prisma skills sync`, which the CLI suggested.\n\nYour colleague's note matched on the version question and on the init, emit and db init steps. Its query API was slightly off: `create` takes the data directly, and nested creates are not supported, so the script creates the posts separately with `authorId`. `ANSWER.md` lists which parts of the note applied and which did not.\n\nFiles are in `/private/tmp/h-45VeRo`: `script.ts`, `ANSWER.md`, `src/prisma/contract.prisma`, and the generated `src/prisma/` files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_de